#
# The ignore list of apps/frontend/Dockerfile. Its build context is the
# repository root, and BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` before
# `<context>/.dockerignore` and never for this path, so
# `Dockerfile.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile is a symlink to this file,
# and this list replaces the root one for this image only.
#
# It is an allow-list: the context holds the workspace manifests,
# @fdp/contracts and this package, and nothing else of the repository — no
# `.env`, no dataset, no other service. Secrets reach the stack through the
# environment only, and the dataset stays out of images as it stays out of Git.

*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages/contracts
!apps/frontend

# Within those, nothing installed, built or left behind by a test run,
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report

# no test suite of this package, which the image never runs,
apps/frontend/test
apps/frontend/e2e

# and never a secret: Vite would read an apps/frontend/.env while it builds.
**/.env
**/.env.*
